	sections = {
		{
			title = "Summary",
			text = [=[Ragefire Chasm is a network of burning caves beneath {link:orgrimmar}Orgrimmar{/link}. Rivers of lava light its tunnels, and the heat of the deep rises through its stone. It is reached by a passage at the bottom of the {link:cleft-of-shadow}Cleft of Shadow{/link}. Few citizens of the capital know what lies beneath their feet. Those who do have reason to fear it, for the chasm is home to savage troggs and to a secret cult that plots the fall of the {link:horde}Horde{/link}.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "Origins",
			text = [=[No chronicle records who first found the chasm, or how deep its tunnels run. The troggs came first. They climbed from the lava-filled depths and claimed the upper caves as their own. Then the Searing Blade came down from the city above, a sect of the {link:shadow-council}Shadow Council{/link} and a sister to the {link:burning-blade}Burning Blade{/link}. The troggs were too weak to drive them out, and the two now share the dark in uneasy hostility.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "The Present Day",
			text = [=[The Searing Blade has made the chasm its sanctum. Its cultists believe themselves the rising generation of the warlocks' art, and they work to turn the loyal folk of {link:orgrimmar}Orgrimmar{/link} to demon worship. Three leaders command them: a felguard, {link:taragaman-the-hungerer}Taragaman the Hungerer{/link}, a warlock, {link:jergosh-the-invoker}Jergosh the Invoker{/link}, and a {link:satyrs}satyr{/link}, {link:bazzalan}Bazzalan{/link}. The troggs of the Ragefire clan still hold the caves near the entrance under their chieftain, {link:oggleflint}Oggleflint{/link}.

The chasm draws the eyes of the whole {link:horde}Horde{/link}. The {link:tauren}tauren{/link} seer {link:magatha-grimtotem}Magatha Grimtotem{/link} sent envoys to make peace with the troggs, and they were slain. One of her servants, {link:maur-raincaller}Maur{/link} Grimtotem, went down to speak with them and never returned. Envoys of the {link:forsaken}Forsaken{/link} want two books of dark spells held by the cultists. Above all, the Warchief {link:thrall}Thrall{/link} watches. The warlock {link:neeru-fireblade}Neeru Fireblade{/link} sends heroes down into the chasm, and Thrall knows exactly why.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "Within the Chasm",
			text = [=[• {b}The Trogg Caves.{/b} Near the entrance, the troggs of the Ragefire clan make their stand. {link:oggleflint}Oggleflint{/link} rules them.
• {b}The Lava Pools.{/b} Deeper in, the tunnels open onto lakes of molten rock, where molten elementals drift over the fire and great earthborers tunnel through the stone. The cultists keep watch among them.
• {b}The Hungerer's Platform.{/b} {link:taragaman-the-hungerer}Taragaman the Hungerer{/link} waits above the fire, the leader the cult shows to the world.
• {b}The Warlock's Chamber.{/b} {link:jergosh-the-invoker}Jergosh the Invoker{/link} works his rites in a chamber of the lower caves.
• {b}The Satyr's Ledge.{/b} Above the warlock's chamber, on a ledge reached by dark ramps, {link:bazzalan}Bazzalan{/link} waits in the shadows.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "Those Who Dwell Below",
			text = [=[The Searing Blade is divided into cultists, enforcers and warlocks, each more dangerous than the last. The body of {link:maur-raincaller}Maur{/link} Grimtotem lies somewhere in the tunnels, still clutching a satchel he would not let go. Most of the cultists do not know the truth: that their true masters above see them only as expendable, and that only two of their leaders are prized.]=],
